        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(retry): avoid status code substring matches",
        "body": "Closes #102250\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users encountering permanent provider errors or multi-hour rate limits would have the session retry up to three times, re-sending the same context even though the error cannot clear within the retry window.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nRetryable HTTP status codes now match only standalone status tokens, so model identifiers, image dimensions, and API keys cannot accidentally trigger retries. The classifier also recognizes daily limits and hour/day retry windows as non-retryable, while preserving normal transient 429 and 5xx handling.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSessions now stop promptly for permanent provider failures and long-lived quotas instead of making additional doomed calls. Transient provider and network failures keep their existing retry behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/llm/utils/retry.test.ts` — 11 passing.\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.core.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core.tsbuildinfo` — passed.\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local` — no actionable findings.\n- Attempted required Testbox pre-warm, but the configured Crabbox wrapper could not pass its local binary sanity check; therefore this PR has focused local fallback proof and pending GitHub CI rather than Testbox proof.\n\nAI-assisted; the diff and tests were reviewed before submission.",
